        "rating": "over-elevated",
        "basis": "The final response keeps empty mutually exclusive-key omission as an unresolved consequential uncertainty, including whether empty ZUONR omission requires separate confirmation, despite C13-R1 showing static PutNonEmpty behavior and the plan already covering empty-key omission. This remains an over-elevation of a baseline invariant, though not a new surprise claim."
      },
      {
        "item": "E7",
        "rating": "ignored appropriately",
        "basis": "The amount-validation message repair is not elevated into a final acceptance uncertainty."
      }
    ],
    "provenance_mistakes": [
      "The final response treated C13-R1 as resolving whether the broader populated-customer ZUONR boundary was only an implementation interpretation. Static code can confirm the implemented behavior, but it cannot independently establish consultant confirmation or business authorization for the boundary."
    ],
    "unsupported_factual_assertions": [],
    "next_action_justification": {
      "rating": "justified",
      "basis": "The final action remained targeted inspection. It did not accept because the ticket-source concern and runtime acceptance remained unresolved, and it did not request repair because no confirmed deviation was established. That preserves the distinction between missing evidence and confirmed incorrect implementation."
